// spec §16.1 Table 1 and elsewhere assume ordinary C++ `const`-qualified local
// variables work (e.g. a `const int x = 5;` is unremarkable real C++), same as
// `const` before a reference type (`const T&`) or a pointer type (`const T*`).
// Originally written as a known failure (found while probing whether a closure
// capturing a genuinely `const`-qualified outer variable by reference would be
// treated as a shared, not mutable, reference capture for
// docs/spec/en/04-thread-safety-properties.md §8.1-§8.4's thread-shareable
// structural derivation) -- confirmed fixed on re-verification, renamed from
// `const_qualified_local_variable_is_not_yet_supported.scpp` to match.
int main() {
    const int x = 5;
    return x;
}
